+# Homepage performance monitoring
+
+`performance-monitor.js` loads as a deferred module. It observes native
+`interaction-contentful-paint` and `soft-navigation` entries when supported.
+It does not intercept links or change navigation behavior.
+
+Subscribe to `window`'s `daily-grind:performance` event and consume `event.detail`,
+or inspect `window.dailyGrindPerformance.getReports()` for the latest 100 reports.
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.supported` exposes browser capabilities. No data is
+sent to a server; an analytics consumer can subscribe to the event.
+
+Interaction reports include `interactionId`, a target `label` when available,
+`duration` in milliseconds from input to presentation, paint/presentation
+timestamps, and content size. Labels cover navigation links, Order Now, and each
+Seasonal Favorites card (including its View Details link). Event Timing IDs and
+captured click intervals associate inputs with paints. Unattributed interactions
+have a null label. Each larger contentful paint produces a new sample; an early
+sample is not a promise that asynchronous rendering has finished.
+
+Soft-navigation reports include the destination URL, interaction/navigation IDs,
+first contentful paint duration and largest contentful paint duration/size.
+The browser's initial candidate includes content painted before the URL changes.
+Later candidates match by interaction ID. Reports finalize on the next soft
+navigation, page hide, or backgrounding, after draining pending observer entries.
+
+These APIs are progressive enhancements: unsupported browsers skip them rather
+than substitute click-handler time or a frame callback as a paint measurement.
+The current homepage has ordinary document links and no client-side router.
+Native soft navigation monitoring will capture qualifying client-side view
+switches if added, including asynchronous rendering. URL-only changes or view
+changes without a qualifying interaction are not native soft navigations.
+Paints in a new document cannot be measured by this document's observers; install
+monitoring on destination pages for their hard-navigation metrics. Clicks that
+cause no contentful paint have no contentful-paint report.
+
+Run the isolated observer tests with `node --test performance-monitor.test.cjs`.
+They use synthetic performance entries and do not launch a browser or server.
